	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>S[alutem] d[ico].</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Accepi non a te, <persName ref="p8312">Cochlee</persName>, sed <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>ab amicis<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1"><persName ref="p1055">Martin Frecht</persName> und <persName ref="p8055">Ambrosius Blarer</persName>; s. <persName ref="p1055">Frechts</persName> Brief an <persName ref="p8178">Blarer</persName> vom 23. September 1543 (Blarer BW II 104f, <ref target="file11076">Nr. 1034</ref>). Über <persName ref="p8178">Blarer</persName> und <persName ref="p1055">Frecht</persName> erfolgte auch die Zustellung von <persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> Brief und Buch an <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName>; s. oben <ref target="file11915">Nr. 1869</ref>; Conradin <hi>Bonorand,</hi> Die Reaktion Bullingers, Joachim Vadians und anderer evangelischer Schweizer auf die antireformatorische Tätigkeit des Johannes Cochläus, in: <bibl source="b289">HBGesA</bibl> II 215-230, bes. 222f.</note>, quem tamen ad me scripsisti <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>libellum<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Vgl. oben <ref target="file11885">Nr. 1839</ref>, Anm. 2.</note>.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Mirabar profecto consilium tuum, <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>qui ad me dignatus esses scribere, <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>at eadem mittere supersedisses.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Caeterum, <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>ubi libellum legere coepissem, mox d[e]<lb xml:id="p1z7"/>prehendi<note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>Randtext beschädigt.</hi></note> post amicam inscriptionem <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>reliqua omnia esse hostilia, ni<lb xml:id="p1z9"/>l aeque expetere te atque responsionem <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>a me saltem aliquam.</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Morem itaque gess[i]<note xml:id="fnc" type="footnote" n="c"><hi>Randtext beschädigt.</hi></note> <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>ac succisivis horis haec ad tua respondi,<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">Vgl. oben <ref target="file11885">Nr. 1839</ref>, Anm. 3.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>quae vides, quae et mitto, ne responsio per <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>omnium manus oberret, priusquam<pb type="edition" next="137"/> ad te <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>veniat, ad quem pertinet maxime.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la" ana="salute">Glor<lb xml:id="p1z15"/>i[am]<note xml:id="fnd" type="footnote" n="d"><hi>Randtext beschädigt.</hi></note> servatoris Iesu, puritatem religionis <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>animarumque salutem me querere <lb xml:id="p1z17"/>novit is, qui nihil nescit.</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Neque ad <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>tua respondi et ita te excepi, ut verit[us]<note xml:id="fne" type="footnote" n="e"><hi>Randtext beschädigt.</hi></note> <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>es,<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">Vgl. <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName>' Epilog zur oben Anm. 2 erwähnten Schrift, bes. f. M2v.: "Quod si vagis elusionibus evadere aut impotentibus tantum conviciis, non rationibus firmis nec scripturae locis ad rem apposite facientibus mihi obviare volueris [...]".</note> sed ita, ut me decere putavi, qui <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>Christo servio et omnes illi adducere cu<lb xml:id="p1z21"/>pio.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Faxit gratia Christi salutaris, ut <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>filio dei syncere cognito in ipso <lb xml:id="p1z23"/>aeternum vivas.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l587">Tiguri</placeName> in <placeName ref="l862">Helv<lb xml:id="p1z24"/>etiis</placeName>, martii 14. anno domini sal<lb xml:id="p1z25"/>vatoris 1544.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z26"/><persName ref="p495">H. Bullingerus</persName>, <placeName ref="l587">Tigurinae</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z27"/>ecclesiae minister.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Ohne Adresse.]</note>
				</p>
			</div>
